  "result": "Perfect! All 270 tests pass. I've successfully added duplicate customer merging functionality:\n\n**Added `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)` to src/customers.js:**\n\n1. **Functionality:**\n   - Removes the `fromId` customer from the customers list\n   - Reassigns all invoices from `fromId` to `intoId`\n   - Returns ok({ customers, invoices }) with updated data\n   - Preserves all other invoice data\n   - Does not modify input arrays (returns new arrays)\n\n2. **Error handling:**\n   - CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if either fromId or intoId isn't in customers\n   - SAME_CUSTOMER if both IDs refer to the same customer (after normalization)\n\n3. **Features:**\n   - Normalizes both customer IDs (trim, uppercase) before processing\n   - Handles multiple invoices from the same customer\n   - Preserves invoices from other customers unchanged\n   - Maintains customer count reduction by exactly one\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- SAME_CUSTOMER error code\n\n**Test coverage (17 new tests):**\n- Customer removal verification\n- Target customer preservation\n- Invoice reassignment\n- Other invoices preservation\n- Same customer error handling\n- Missing fromId error handling\n- Missing intoId error handling\n- Customer ID normalization (case insensitive, whitespace trimmed)\n- Empty invoice list handling\n- Multiple invoices from same customer\n- Invoice data preservation (except customerId)\n- Input array immutability\n- Customer count reduction\n- Mixed invoices (multiple customers)\n- Return value structure verification\n- Case-insensitive same customer detection\n\nAll 270 tests pass!",
